# No Emojis Policy

## Absolute Ban on Emojis
- **NEVER use emojis anywhere in the codebase**, including UI components, templates, styles, script logic, notifications, user messages, share texts, or console output.
- Emojis are considered a lazy shortcut for visual effects.
- Always use a considered CSS approach with refined animations, colors, micro-badges, SVG vectors, or icon fonts (e.g. PrimeIcons `pi pi-*`).

## Implementation Standards
- **Icons**: Use SVG icons or icon fonts (`pi pi-*` from PrimeIcons) with precise sizing and color inheritance.
- **Status & Streaks**: Use CSS glow animations, color transitions, keyframes (e.g., pulsing flame or streak badges), and semantic tokens.
- **Indicators & Feedback**: Use dedicated CSS classes (e.g. `.mm-match-higher`, `.mm-match-lower`, `.mm-match-exact`) with subtle background tints and borders.
- **Country Badges**: Use styled ISO two-letter text tags (e.g., `<span class="mm-country-badge">US</span>`) styled with micro-typography and subtle borders instead of flag emojis.
- **Share & Export Text**: Use clean structured text (brackets, dividers, percentages, ratios) without emoji decorations.
